    "reading_order": 12,
    "text": "As p(–1) = 0 and p(4) = 0, –1 and 4 are called the zeroes of the quadratic\npolynomial x2 – 3x – 4. More generally, a real number k is said to be a zero of a\npolynomial p(x), if p(k) = 0.",
